window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Two weeks ago, I finalized a divorce from a man who spent five years deceiving me. Now, I'm embracing a new chapter and another chance at the life I want.</p> <p>To celebrate being single, I decide to take a spontaneous trip with my sister to <b><i>Capri, Italy.</i></b></p> <p>No itinerary. No plans. Only a promise to see where Capri takes us.</p> <p>Little did I know it would be on a yacht with a handsome stranger.</p> <p>Jones Archer is thirteen years older and dangerously charming.</p> <p>He’s also a man who knows what he wants and has his sights set on me.</p> <p>We agree to one week of uninterrupted pleasure. No personal exchanges. No talk about the future.</p> <p><b><i>Just us.</i></b></p> <p>But there’s one thing I’m worried about—feelings. I’m not wired to ignore them. Especially when Jones makes me second guess everything I thought I knew about love.</p> <p><i>(Capri is a standalone summertime romance with an HEA).</i></p> <p>Check content warnings prior: miscarriage/loss of a child + dementia.</p>"; 
